o all our intentions, encamp the army. Having been fatigued, we shall cross the ocean-going Gangā on the morrow.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.435,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-83-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2077020","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"24071f7c84af394e0061f028111de9089d17b4bab86c97170b20f9f59d58bdae","compact":"296a6c17e44e897866df98eb33ee0e638894c3d833449e77a09680800122cc7b","nasal":"025ae81e7a15786e2fd3f43be3fa895fc06760af3160384d287658b18993426c"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-77-21","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":77,"verse":21,"english":"Having crossed the stream, I am anxious to offer its water to the monarch, who has gone to heaven in behalf of his spiritual body.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-83-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2077021","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"514a96270c286ceacc469f90745b424914bb302a426242e146d36e3309334307","compact":"dc3c01d204383d0e6a13a419f9f07e83de9d78a59f00629085778698234cfc39","nasal":"dc3c01d204383d0e6a13a419f9f07e83de9d78a59f00629085778698234cfc39"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-77-22","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":77,"verse":22,"english":"When he had said this, the courtiers with collected minds saying, “Be it so,” disposed their forces, each according to his wish.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-83-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2077022","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2da97816fe86915eddfd721d25b5efecf282776c6f6ec5a107c5731c2301a162","compact":"02f005f91101d3a7e56ddf607aea2f4012d1a37c7995d588cc87cbb06b767b13","nasal":"d7912c203bb6666478b27fcf022359358a68446a9e6150c701792132461f5280"}}